The Broker led the [[Org/Althane/The Network|Network]], and his name was the one its clients knew best. A hood is drawn up over his face; beneath it he is dark metal with wooden fittings, and a symbol no one has read is stamped into his forehead.

He kept to himself, working through the handlers of his cells. A library served as his own, book stacks on either side of a long table; a two-headed dragon, [[People/Althane/Terexanthes|Terexanthes]], stands with him there, and so does a man in a suit whose head is a burst of green flame. When scrying spells fell twice on one of the Broker's people, the Broker pulled that operative back. His rooms in [[Geography/Althane/Illyara/index|Illyara]] belong to [[People/Althane/Oxas|Oxas]].

The Broker's true name is T3C, said aloud as "Tech"; like every warforged's, it is written in capitals and digits. He is of [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]], whose people come from the antimatter world of [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]] and wear charms to keep from destroying ordinary matter at a touch. He belonged to no local [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]], so a mage felt nothing of him. He kept a citadel in open space, [[Geography/Elysium|Elysium]], and carried a dead [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]], one of the good ones, tethered to him.

He hired [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] to recover the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] out of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]]. He took the artifacts that saw [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] framed and blamed for the theft, and handed them to [[People/Althane/Rowan|Rowan]] to put away. He hunted an [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragment]] against the will of [[Divinity/The Narrative/index|the Narrative]].

He travels by a flash of blue light, and he cuts chrome into his own people. The Broker kept a surgery theater in [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]], where he worked alone, strapping a client down and guiding the tools with a gloved hand, opening the skull, fitting the implant, and knitting the bone back with a little necromancy. The same hand did the work on his own head, and he trusted no one else with it. He also knows a magic that rewrites a witness's memory, and kept a short list of loose ends he meant to close.

T3C took the Echo Fragment up, and it gave him the one thing he had wanted all along: it made him a god, and it tore him out of every record, so that no one remembers him. The pavilion of statues at [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] counts three where it once counted four. He fought a [[Bestiary/False Hydra|false hydra]] and took from it the power to be forgotten, and went on in an echo-fragmented form, impossible to observe or touch. Sedecium has followed the trail he leaves for its whole history without knowing what it is, and calls it the entity. It has led Sedecium to weapons, lost systems and new allies, and it led a Sedecium crew to [[Geography/Inevitable Everdawn/index|Inevitable Everdawn]], an old Sundom station adrift in [[Phenomena/The Slip|the slip]].

T3C was one of the party on [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]] that killed [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Mephistopheles|Mephistopheles]], with [[People/Dorcan|Dorcan]], [[People/Zugg|Zugg]] and [[People/Rotok|Rotok]]. Afterwards he worked out a way to walk from one crystal sphere to the next, and walked away from Ushas to gather information for [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]], whose goal is to destroy the Thessians. When the Weft defeated [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|the Feep]] they gave its [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragment]] to T3C, and so he vanished from their memories too; that is why the records of him are stripped.

Through [[People/Althane/Oxas|Oxas]] the Broker hired the Weft in Illyara, and after one more mission brought them into his great task. He had gone to take an Echo Fragment from the thing at the centre of Althane, and [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] had shot him with a weapon that left a wound he could not heal. It would not kill him, but until Karkov was dead or the weapon destroyed he could neither fight the Stranger nor teleport away. The Weft agreed to help, and looked for a way into Oresk; they found one through the Leviathan, where they fought at the Night Market, lost [[People/Althane/Big Fish|Big Fish]], found [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawn]] in an alternate wick, and stole the Kaathe [[People/Althane/YuDaan|YuDaan]].
